# What must never enter the build context.
#
# `COPY . /app` in brain.Dockerfile means everything here is a decision about
# what ends up baked into an image layer — and an image layer is not something
# you can quietly delete later. This file mirrors .gitignore's credential block
# for the same reason that block exists: the patterns have to be here BEFORE the
# secret is, not after.

# Secrets. `.env` alone missed every variant a person actually creates.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credential file shapes, wherever they land.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.token
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*credentials*.json
secrets/

# Local-only operator working files. They are excluded from the PUBLIC
# .gitignore on purpose, so without these three lines `COPY . /app` bakes them
# into the image — the one artifact this project must never publish.
CLAUDE.md
JOURNAL.md
.claude

# Runtime state and history: never useful in an image, and data/ carries every
# run's output including whatever a tool retained.
.git
data
*.db
capabilities_store/_artifacts

# Build and environment noise.
.venv
build
dist
*.egg-info
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
.pytest_cache
